    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.starter \r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nThe mini.starter `echo()` function hard codes the `WarningMsg` hl group for the `'(mini.starter)'` text that appears before echo's log messages [link to source](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/eb0f557a5797cfe9c720ed84a71582c22bccb4f8/lua/mini/starter.lua#L1490) . I propose that a new highlight group is created (potentially called `MiniStarterEchoHeader`) that links to `WarningMsg` allowing color schemes to customize the color of this log message header. \r\n\r\nI think this should be considered because currently colorscheme maintainers cannot customize this prompt without effecting all warning messages for all plugins, and the mini.starter echos are not always actually warnings so it would be nice if they did not have to use warning colors. \r\n\r\nI would be  interested in helping implement this feature if this feature request is approved, and help is wanted :)\r\n\r\n> The orange text in the bottom left is what I would like to customize with my colorscheme [lackluster.nvim](https://github.com/slugbyte/lackluster.nvim)\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/baa70942-dc87-4f1f-ac19-f585c75a0abb)\r\n\r\n",
