        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThe major problem in having this done is that the same approach is used in 10 modules in total. All of them have `(mini.xxx)` prefix whenever the text is `echo`ed and highlighted as a `WarningMsg`.\r\n\r\nCase can be made that 'mini.starter' (and probably 'mini.align') use them not for one time messages but for user interaction. I am not yet sure how strong of a case that this. Currently preserving all modules to behave in the same way feels like a stronger argument, but I'll think about it.",
